WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.935
-Democrats screamed
over each other

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.137
in a chaotic debate

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.572
as President Trump tightens

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.139
his authoritarian grip on power.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.308
For more on this,
it's time "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.712
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.779
[ Whistling ]

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.315
The 2020 election
will be a referendum

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.317
on whether we wanna preserve
whatever's left

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.919
of our Democratic institutions

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.089
or whether we wanna complete
the slide into authoritarianism

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.090
we've seen under Donald Trump.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.791
And that slide is not only real,

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:29.161
after Trump's impeachment
acquittal, it's accelerating.

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:31.464
You can tell both from Trump's
increased lawlessness

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.732
and from the way he stands.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.733
I mean, look at him.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.768
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.570
He leans like he's accelerating.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.740
He literally looks like
he's sliding downhill on skis.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.809
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.244
If you gave him a tiny push,

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.946
he'd fall over
like a Jenga tower.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.648
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.317
The Trump White House
has literally been making lists

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.152
of supposedly disloyal
government officials,

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.854
purging them
from the administration,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.657
installing unqualified cronies
in high-profile positions,

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.961
insisting he has the right
to interfere in criminal cases

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.929
to protect his allies
and claiming

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.831
that, not only is he
above the law,

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:08.134
but that he, himself,
is the law.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.269
-I'm allowed to be
totally involved.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.071
I'm actually, I guess,

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.974
the chief law enforcement
officer of the country.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.842
[ Laughter ]
-No! You're not

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:18.444
a law enforcement officer.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:21.714
First of all, you'd never pass
the background check.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.515
[ Laughter ]
Or the physical.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:25.518
[ Laughter ]
You don't --

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:29.756
[ Cheering and applause ]
You don't even know --

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.492
You don't even know
the sound a gun makes.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.661
-Ah ah ah, bink!

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:38.531
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Is that a gun

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:41.868
or a duck's mouth?

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.503
[as Trump]
Beak!

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.871
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.672
Also, Trump declaring himself

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.607
the country's chief
law enforcement officer

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:51.110
makes clear that he desperately
wishes he was a cop,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.378
when, at best, he's more like
that weird crossing guard

00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:54.647
who no one actually knows

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.981
[ Laughter ]
and who doesn't seem

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:57.583
to be paying attention
to traffic.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:58.650
[as Trump]
Alright, kids, let's go.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.319
Just make sure --
Dodge the cars.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.789
[ Laughter and applause ]
And, by the way,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.024
while he's tightening his own
authoritarian grip on power,

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.659
Trump is fresh
off a trip to India,

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.595
where he cozied up to another
authoritarian nationalist,

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:12.264
Narendra Modi, who's rounded up
thousands of Muslims

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.901
and passed a citizenship law
that discriminates against Islam

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.702
and, rather than comment
on any of that,

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.038
Trump said, in a press
conference before he left India,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.040
that he wanted
to avoid being controversial,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.608
so as not to ruin his trip.

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:23.877
-I thought it was
a great two days.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.045
It was a fantastic two days.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.114
I'm gonna be not
at all controversial

00:02:29.114 --> 00:02:30.750
because I don't wanna
blow the two days,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.418
plus two days of travel,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.554
[ Laughter ]
on one answer,
one little answer.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.689
So I'll be very conservative
of my answers,

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.124
if you don't mind.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.426
-It's so weird when Trump just
openly says what he's doing.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.628
[ Laughter ]
He's like a guy
on a date saying...

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:43.997
[as Trump]
Normally, I'd be cheap,

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.331
but, tonight,
I'm gonna pick up the tab

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.699
so you'll have sex with me.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.936
But, tomorrow,
breakfast is on you.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.805
[ Laughter ]
Trump, of course,
has a deep affinity

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.806
for fellow authoritarians.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.174
He's always trying to mimic them

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.443
or impress them,
whether it's Modi or Putin

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.111
or the time he sat
in the Oval Office

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:01.247
with Crown Prince
Mohammad bin Salman

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.249
of Saudi Arabia
and literally showed off

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.484
a giant poster of all the
weapons he'd sold to them,

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.420
like a sixth grader presenting

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.488
[ Laughter and applause ]
a class project on the military.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.859
[as Trump]
Did you know the Army has
planes and tanks and boats?

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.094
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.763
The Democrats are tryin'
to sort out

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.530
who has the best chance
of defeating Trump

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.366
and, thankfully, we got answers

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.168
to that important question
last night,

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.904
in a calm, well-organized
debate on CBS

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.438
[ Laughter ]
with clear questions,

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.041
in which everyone
took turns speaking

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.775
and we all got to hear
their answers.

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.911
-First of all -- No.
-Bernie, let me go.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.178
Let me go.
-I think -- Tom,

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:35.480
I think she was talkin'
about my plan, not yours.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.915
[ Voices overlapping ]

00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:38.250
-The opposition
to the filibuster

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.685
-Time out.
-is not a discretion

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.120
from a long time ago.
-I think she recognized me.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.288
-Mayor Bloomberg,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.423
it is alleged you have said
-Never said that.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:45.758
to one of his --
-Oh come on.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.493
I wrote that law.
-That bill, along with --

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.461
[ Applause ]
You didn't write that bill.

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:50.630
-I did write.
-I wrote that bill.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.864
-I wrote the bill. Let's talk
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.365
about what it adds up to.
-Let's talk about math.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:54.467
-Let's talk
about math,

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.568
indeed. Okay.
-Let's talk about math.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.736
-So here's the math.
-If we do nothing,

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.070
-Things that you have --
-the truth is, Pete --

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.538
-One at a time.
-The Americans --

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.207
-Donald -- Donald Trump
-Senator Klobuchar.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.942
-[Shouting]
Bernie. Bernie. Donald Trump --
-This has to stop.

00:04:03.942 --> 00:04:05.310
-Let me answer.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.813
-Reparations and I challenge --
-Thank you, Bill.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.315
Senator Klobuchar, question.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.517
-Records for that,
for this whole campaign.
-New topic. New topic, Senator.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.919
-Jesus!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:17.756
Does the C in CBS stand
for cluster[bleep]?

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:19.291
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:23.196
[ Cheering ]
That was --

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.297
I mean --

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.399
That was like watching
a family dinner

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.735
if the special ingredient
in the mashed potatoes

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.968
was cocaine.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.070
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.538
I've seen more
polite conversations

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.873
between New Yorkers
fighting over a cab.

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:36.075
"Hey, I was here first!"
"Oh, yeah?

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.677
Then why was my hand up?!"

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:38.978
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.180
Now, with the stakes
for the 2020 election so high,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.482
the Democrat candidates
spent some time, in particular,

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:45.551
fighting over their own
positions on foreign policy.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.587
Now, let's be clear --
There's no comparison to Trump

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.722
on this topic
and any false equivalence

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.891
between Trump and any Democrat
is absurd.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.692
I mean, Trump has taken
his praise for dictators

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.294
to gross new levels,
emulating them

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.430
and even bragging
that he and Kim Jong-un

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.632
"fell in love"
over Kim's beautiful letters,

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.768
which he has bragged about
or shown off to reporters

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:03.869
multiple times.

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:06.305
Trump loves holding up
pieces of paper.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.441
[ Laughter ]
He's like a high school senior

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.442
running into the house with his
college acceptance letter.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:13.546
[as Trump]
Mom, look! I got
into Pyongyang University!

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.781
[ Laughter ]
At least that's what it says.

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.550
I can't read.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.218
And, yet, even as Trump
has lavished praise

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.086
on one authoritarian
nationalist after another,

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:23.856
Republicans and Democrats
were attacking Bernie Sanders

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.825
for comments in which
he praised, not Cuba,

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.193
but Cuba's literacy program.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.994
Now, as fact-checkers
have noticed,

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:30.930
Sanders' comments
about Cuba mirror those

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.265
of President Barack Obama
in 2017,

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:34.600
soon after he had moved

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.436
to open diplomatic
relations with Cuba

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.437
and, yet, when Bernie tried
to point that out

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:39.839
in last night's
Democratic debate,

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.274
a few people in the crowd
tried to boo him,

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:43.376
to Bernie's surprise.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:46.445
-What I said
is what Barack Obama said,

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.013
in terms of Cuba.

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:51.484
That Cuba made progress
on education.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.419
Yes, I think --
[ Booing ]

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.887
Really?!
-Yes!

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.155
-Really?!

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.223
[ Laughter ]
-Bernie Sounds like

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.991
he just got cut in line
at the deli.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.325
[as Sanders]
Really?!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:00.325 --> 00:06:01.427
You're gonna walk up?

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.561
Let me see your ticket.

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:04.330
That's handwritten!
That's handwritten!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.630
That's not from this store!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.170
Meanwhile, billionaire former
Republican Michael Bloomberg

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.139
has actually praised
authoritarian leaders,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:16.576
like China's Xi Jinping, who he
has said is not a dictator.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.345
And, last night, Bloomberg again
refused to call Xi a dictator,

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:21.714
but, somehow, even worse
than his comments

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.383
on a repressive dictator
was his bungling

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:26.285
of multiple, lame,
prewritten jokes

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.154
that he tried to shoehorn
into his answers.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:29.822
-Mayor Bloomberg,
as mayor of New York,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.423
you declared war on obesity.

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:33.792
You banned trance fats
from restaurants

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:36.295
and you tried to do the same
with large sugary drinks.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.164
So, if you become president,

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:41.467
will you push those policies
on the national level as well?

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.335
-Well, I think what's right
for New York City

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:44.537
isn't necessarily right
-[Cough]

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.272
for all the other cities,
otherwise, you'd have

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.073
a Naked Cowboy in every city.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:50.309
[ Laughter ]
So, let's get serious, here.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:53.212
Redlining is not the problem
with the mortgage market,

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:55.547
but it was a problem for the
communities where it was done

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:56.549
and we stopped that.

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.117
Let me also say,

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:01.053
just since I have
the floor for a second,

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:03.623
that I really am surprised
that all of these --

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:07.259
my fellow contestants
up here, I guess,

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:08.427
would be the right word for it,

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:10.162
[ Laughter ]
given nobody pays attention

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:11.530
to the clock.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.899
I'm surprised they show up
because I would've thought,

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.401
after I did such a good job
in beating them last week,

00:07:16.401 --> 00:07:19.305
that they'd be a little bit
afraid to do that.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:22.374
-[dully] Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.374 --> 00:07:24.843
Let me put this in terms
a New Yorker would understand.

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:26.679
Mike Bloomberg went so far
out of his way

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:30.282
to make that joke, he had
to take the FDR to the BQE,

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:32.217
[ Laughter ]
accidentally ended up
on the LIE,

00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:34.252
and, now, his competitors
are all [laughing] on the FU.

00:07:34.252 --> 00:07:35.554
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:39.091
Now, Mike Bloomberg
could just have easily stayed

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.593
out of the race
and spent his money

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.228
to help whichever Democrat
got the nomination

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:45.064
or he coulda just offered Trump
himself the money to resign.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.065
You know Trump would take it.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.599
Trump has never, in his life,

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:49.068
passed up an opportunity
to make money.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.670
If you asked him to sell
the presidency for $1 billion,

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.707
he'd say yes and then quietly
peel the sticker off his desk

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.542
that says, "For sale, $10."

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.477
[ Laughter ]
And, yet, Bloomberg decided,

00:07:58.477 --> 00:07:59.845
instead, to get
into the race himself

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:02.315
because he cares more
about stopping progressives,

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.883
like Elizabeth Warren
and Bernie Sanders.

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:06.552
In fact, he basically
admitted as much himself

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:09.388
in leaked audio from 2016,
in which CNN reported

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:11.057
that he called Warren scary.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:13.358
Honestly, the way Warren has
destroyed him in the debates,

00:08:13.358 --> 00:08:14.360
he should be scared.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.694
[ Laughter ]
Last night, for example,

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:17.997
she highlighted allegations
that Bloomberg harassed

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.465
and discriminated
against pregnant women

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.633
in his company,
including one incident

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:23.636
in which he allegedly told
a pregnant employee,

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.504
"Kill it."
Now, Bloomberg denied

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.773
making the remark, even though
The Washington Post reported

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:29.375
that a former Bloomberg
employee said

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:32.244
he witnessed the conversation
and then, after the debate,

00:08:32.244 --> 00:08:35.381
MSNBC anchor Chris Matthews
asked Warren

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:37.183
if she thought Bloomberg
was lying

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:40.553
and her straightforward answer
seemed to confuse Matthews.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.788
-Do you believe that
the former mayor of New York

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.523
said that
to a pregnant employee?

00:08:44.523 --> 00:08:46.692
-Well, a pregnant employee
sure said that he did.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.293
Why shouldn't I believe her?

00:08:48.293 --> 00:08:49.928
-You believe he's lying.

00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:50.996
-I believe the woman.

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:52.197
-You believe he's lying.
-Which means he's

00:08:52.197 --> 00:08:54.066
not telling the truth.
-And why would he lie?

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.301
Because just to protect himself.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:56.568
-Yeah.

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:58.670
And why would she lie?

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.406
I mean, that's
the question, Chris!

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.474
[ Laughter ]
-Damn! Look at his face!

00:09:02.474 --> 00:09:06.278
[ Laughter and applause ]
He genuinely can't understand.

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:07.979
[as Matthews]
Why would he lie,
just to protect himself?

00:09:07.979 --> 00:09:10.015
Doesn't make any sense!
Powerful men never do that!

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:12.985
[ Laughter ]
Warren flipped the question
on him perfectly.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:14.586
As soon as she turned it
around on him,

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:16.455
Matthews malfunctioned
like a robot

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.490
who'd been asked
an unsolvable riddle.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.460
"Could God make a rock so big,
he could not lift it?"

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.928
[as Matthews]
Error. Error!

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:24.363
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.697
We're watching
as our current president

00:09:25.697 --> 00:09:26.998
tightens his grip on power

00:09:26.998 --> 00:09:29.234
and cozies up to authoritarians
around the world.

00:09:29.234 --> 00:09:31.003
Meanwhile,
an ex-Republican billionaire

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:33.172
is trying to buy his way
into the Democratic primary,

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:34.940
because he's scared
of progressives

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.341
like Warren and Bernie.

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:38.844
And, when Bloomberg insists he's
the only one who can beat Trump,

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.579
the rest of the field looks
at him and says...

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:42.481
-Really?
-Yes!

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:43.682
-Really?!
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.682 --> 00:09:44.749
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:44.749 --> 00:09:48.554
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

